G, that uses a skeletal framework from a game called Freeform Universal, but really that is just the very basic bones and the game is much, much, different than normal Freeform Universals structure. It is a pretty rules light, and narrative forward type game. The rules aren&#39;t complicated, and creating a die pool is supposed to be fast, and encourage a player to use their imagination/creativity to make each action interesting and different... At least that is its intention.</p><p>I would like to point out a few things: I am not a writer, a designer, or more importantly: An editor. This &quot;manuscript&quot; needs... A <strong><em>lot</em></strong> of work before it is anywhere near where I would like it to be for a more &quot;official&quot; offering. It is missing information from certain areas of the text- like advice for helping the narrator come up with scenes, episodes, arcs, and seasons. However, all of the core gameplay elements are present in the document. This thing needs a lot of polish, and quite frankly hasn&#39;t been playtested. However, since I don&#39;t have a steady group of guinea pi... I mean Players *Cough*, I really don&#39;t have a lot of ways of playtesting it myself.</p><p>So with that in mind, and in that spirit, I leave it to the whims of the individuals of the forum to do with as they please for now! If I make sweeping, drastic changes to the game as I go, I might post them up here for those interested as time goes on. Of course, feedback is appreciated, but I solely ask that we keep it constructive, and to the point and keep in mind that we might not share the same opinions on what makes for a good superhero game- which is more than okay!</p><p>Okay, I&#39;m done now I promise. Have fun kids! (Also, I hate the current title and I am certainly looking for a good alternative that isn&#39;t already taken so the current title is a work in progress...)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
